    "https://jobs.anu.edu.au/jobs/postdoctoral-fellow-canberra-act-act-australia-32d81648-860c-4173-948d-9ff36ec44f6b": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Fellow - Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia Privacy Statement People & Culture Information for applicants Salaries & benefits Respect and Inclusion Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander employment Applicant Login Kiosk mode Postdoctoral Fellow Postdoctoral Fellow 563454 Canberra / ACT, ACT, Australia, 2601 Fixed Term Closing at: Oct 4 2026 - 23:55 AEDT Add to favourites View favourites Position Description Classification: Academic Level A Salary package : $91,546 - $114,906 per annum plus 17% superannuation Terms : 2 x Full-time, Fixed Term, (up to 24 months) The Malins group in the Research School of Chemistry are seeking up to two Postdoctoral Fellows in synthetic organic chemistry and peptide chemistry to support activities associated with the Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Advanced Peptide and Protein Engineering (CAPE) and the Snow Fellowship Program. The Positions The first position is a fixed-term, up to 24‑month appointment supporting research in the Malins Lab associated with the Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Advanced Peptide and Protein Engineering (CAPE) and focusing on the chemical synthesis of modified peptides and proteins. The role will involve the initiation and execution of collaborative projects with both academic and industry partners. The second position is a fixed‑term, 24‑month appointment to support research initiatives in the Malins Lab associated with the Snow Fellowship Program on the development of novel peptide-based therapeutics. The role requires expertise in organic synthesis, peptide chemistry and chemical biology and will involve the synthesis of bioactive peptides, the examination of their chemical reactivity, and the optimisation of their drug-like properties. The People The successful applicants will undertake independent research in organic and medicinal chemistry with a view to publishing original and innovative results in refereed journals, presenting their work at seminars and conferences, and collaborating with other researchers. The successful applicants will hold a relevant PhD (or awarding of a PhD within six months of appointment commencement) with a track record of innovative research in peptide chemistry. Applicants should demonstrate experience across organic chemistry and peptide synthesis, including compound purification and characterisation. The School/Department The Research School of Chemistry is a leading centre of chemistry research in Australia. Researchers have a tradition of excellence in addressing the world’s most pressing chemistry issues, including challenges in medicinal chemistry and chemical biology. The College/Division The ANU College of Science and Medicine (CoSM) encompasses the disciplines of: Astronomy and Astrophysics, Biology, Chemistry, Earth Sciences, Medical Research, Medicine and Psychology, and Physics. Staff and students within the ANU College of Science and Medicine conduct research and deliver a research-led education program that encompasses the entire breadth of the sciences, supported by extensive international networks and by world-class facilities. For further information please contact, Professor Lara Malins, ARC Future Fellow, T: +612 6125 9106 E: Lara.malins@anu.edu.au. The University actively encourages applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. For more information on employment opportunities, contact our Indigenous Employment Consultant on indigenous.employment@anu.edu.au. ANU values diversity and inclusion and is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to those of all backgrounds and identities. For more information about staff equity at ANU, visit https://services.anu.edu.au/human-resources/respect-inclusion Application information In order to apply for this role please make sure that you upload the following documents: A statement addressing the selection criteria. A current curriculum vitae (CV) which includes the names and contact details of at least three referees (preferably including a current or previous supervisor). If your CV does not include referees, you can complete these online when prompted in the application form. Applications which do not address the selection criteria may not be considered for the position. Please note: The preferred candidate will be required to complete mandatory pre-employment declarations and background checks relevant to the role they have applied for, in accordance with the Background Checking Procedure and the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-Based Violence . Job referral Know someone great for this role! Recommended Jobs Research Software Engineer (Female Identified Position) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Develop innovative scientific software and support advanced climate modelling as a Research Software Engineer. Senior WHS Specialist Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead complex WHS and biosafety programs, providing specialist advice, governance, risk management and safety assurance. Senior Research Software Engineer (Female Identified Position) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Lead development of scientific software for climate modelling, HPC and data-driven research as a Senior Research Software Engineer. Institute Administrator Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Join the Global Institute for Women’s Leadership in a varied role supporting projects, operations and administration while delivering social impact WHS Consultant Injury Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Provide procedural, injury prevention and injury management services and administration to facilitate effective implementation of the University WHS Management System. Senior Consultant, User Experience (HR Systems Projects) Canberra / ACT, ACT, 2601 Create user-friendly HR systems documentation and websites, improving navigation, usability and stakeholder experience. Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device I do not accept I accept"
